        "id": 22089,
        "name": "evandan457",
        "username": "evandan457",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/5e9695/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2011-09-16T15:05:11.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>That’s gonna get pretty wild if you guys are actually gonna have four expansions, totaling 20 villains, 20 environments, and 18 heroes. But so what you’re saying is the expansions will have rules different from the ones right now? Or will the gameplay be the same as now, in that it’s heroes vs. villains in villain, heroes, environment turn order? I can’t think of any ideas of how the game could be run differently, but I’m sure you guys can think of something. After all, that’s what you do, and you do it pretty well. I’m cool with the heroes vs. villains mode we’ve got now, and I’m assuming it will always be heroes vs. villains, but I’ll be really impressed if the expansions throw in some new game mode or mechanics. Do something with that whole “multiverse” concept you all have going on or something.</p>\n<p>Oh, and just a minor thing, how are these expansions going to be packaged? Is it gonna be like the original box, but just smaller with different art? I’m just trying to plan on how I’m going to store all these cards.</p>",
